WEBVTT

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:17.392
Futurama presents...

00:00:20.996 --> 00:00:23.582
Brought to you by
Mutual of Omicron.

00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:27.377
Insuring your world,
and its destruction.

00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:31.465
Tonight's planet,
a primitive backwater known only as...

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.175
Earth.

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:44.478
Of all
the creatures on Earth,

00:00:44.561 --> 00:00:48.815
none has a more thrilling life cycle
than the intrepid salmon.

00:00:49.358 --> 00:00:52.235
It all begins in a cold,
freshwater stream,

00:00:52.319 --> 00:00:54.029
where the salmon
eggs incubate.

00:00:54.863 --> 00:00:56.156
I'm born, baby!

00:00:56.448 --> 00:00:59.117
The new hatchlings
are known as "fry."

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:00.702
What's your name?

00:01:00.786 --> 00:01:02.746
I don't have a name.
I'm a salmon.

00:01:03.246 --> 00:01:05.248
After three years
in the stream,

00:01:05.332 --> 00:01:08.919
the young salmon are ready
for the arduous journey to the ocean.

00:01:09.294 --> 00:01:12.547
I do look forward to
cavorting in the spray.

00:01:12.631 --> 00:01:16.969
The trip will be dangerous.
Only three in 10 will survive.

00:01:17.052 --> 00:01:19.221
Let's all 10 of
us go together.

00:01:19.304 --> 00:01:21.890
There's safety in numbers.

00:01:24.309 --> 00:01:27.271
Mm. I reckon my boy
will be right pleased

00:01:27.354 --> 00:01:29.731
when I regurgitate
that into his mouth.

00:01:30.899 --> 00:01:35.946
Looming ahead, nature's waterfall,
the cliff of the waters.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.155
Ah.

00:01:37.281 --> 00:01:40.409
It sure is relaxing
getting swept along by this current.

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.077
Whoa!

00:01:43.078 --> 00:01:44.288
Oh, my!

00:01:45.122 --> 00:01:46.540
Oh, dear!

00:01:47.082 --> 00:01:48.375
Oh, yes!

00:01:51.128 --> 00:01:54.548
This just in.
Three dead in foamy plunge.

00:01:59.303 --> 00:02:03.932
Still, six out of 10 alive.
That's considered good for our species!

00:02:04.099 --> 00:02:06.852
Five out of 10, also nice.

00:02:07.477 --> 00:02:08.520
Yep.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:13.525
And so the salmon
reach the ocean, birthplace of all life.

00:02:14.026 --> 00:02:15.235
Except the salmon.

00:02:17.738 --> 00:02:19.448
Hello. Who are you?

00:02:19.531 --> 00:02:20.616
I'm a salmon.

00:02:20.699 --> 00:02:22.034
Really? Me, too!

00:02:22.117 --> 00:02:23.243
No way!

00:02:23.452 --> 00:02:26.121
So, hey, I don't
want to be too forward,

00:02:26.204 --> 00:02:29.291
but I'd like to mate with you in a few
years when we're sexually mature.

00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:30.500
I'd like that.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:31.793
Oh!

00:02:31.877 --> 00:02:35.797
What have we here?
I'm a Pisces. And you?

00:02:35.881 --> 00:02:38.175
Also Pisces.
We're all Pisces.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:41.511
Then it's a date.
I'll see you at spawning time.

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:44.264
No, thanks.
I've already found my mate.

00:02:47.851 --> 00:02:50.938
You haven't
ignored the last of me.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.672
Having reached maturity,
it is time for the salmon to spawn.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.675
Thus begins their
1000-mile journey

00:03:19.758 --> 00:03:22.344
back to the exact stream
in which they were born.

00:03:22.594 --> 00:03:24.429
So how do we
find our way home?

00:03:24.513 --> 00:03:25.931
Nobody knows!

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:29.810
Experts are unsure whether
salmon navigate by memory,

00:03:29.893 --> 00:03:34.523
sense of smell, or by detecting
variations in Earth's magnetic field.

00:03:34.773 --> 00:03:37.484
Okay, everybody do
one of those three things.

00:03:47.119 --> 00:03:49.579
Well, this is it.
Home, stream home.

00:03:49.663 --> 00:03:53.375
No, it isn't!
I was born in the next stream up.

00:03:55.669 --> 00:03:58.046
You're from
Next Stream Up? So am I!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.966
I can tell by
the magnets in my head, or whatever.

00:04:01.091 --> 00:04:02.175
Let's go!

00:04:02.926 --> 00:04:05.470
The urge to spawn
drives the salmon

00:04:05.595 --> 00:04:08.140
inexorably toward
the stream of its birth.

00:04:09.308 --> 00:04:12.894
Stupid body! Why won't you go
to that other stream?

00:04:12.978 --> 00:04:14.479
Nobody knows!

00:04:14.563 --> 00:04:16.023
I just told you!

00:04:16.732 --> 00:04:19.443
Goodbye! It was fun
maturing with you,

00:04:19.526 --> 00:04:21.153
but at this point
in my life cycle,

00:04:21.236 --> 00:04:23.655
I need a mate who's
within squirting distance.

00:04:24.281 --> 00:04:26.825
I'll never forget you, fish.

00:04:27.242 --> 00:04:31.997
Come on, loxy lady, it's time for
us to get naughty by nature!

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.875
No!

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:55.020
Well, here goes something...

00:04:56.521 --> 00:04:57.606
Don't make it...
Don't make it!

00:04:58.106 --> 00:05:00.317
Ouch.

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:02.611
Son of a fish!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.702
Jumping is for suckers.

00:05:14.957 --> 00:05:17.459
I'm good!
Who wants a piece of me?

00:05:17.626 --> 00:05:19.461
I'll try a bite!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.469
Having completed
its perilous journey,

00:05:27.803 --> 00:05:31.473
the exhausted salmon
enters the final phase of its life cycle.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.978
The female deposits her eggs
and the male fertilizes them.

00:05:36.103 --> 00:05:38.397
Okay, who's next?

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.524
There's a lot more
where that came from!

00:05:44.653 --> 00:05:46.905
I can't see them anymore!
What if they're mating?

00:05:46.989 --> 00:05:49.449
Who cares?
Just release your milt already!

00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:50.742
Everybody's doing it!

00:05:50.826 --> 00:05:53.203
No! I refuse
to release anything

00:05:53.287 --> 00:05:56.498
unless it's in the vicinity of the eggs
of the fish I love!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.716
Tell my offspring I
loved me very much...

00:06:12.347 --> 00:06:15.142
Oh, yeah.
Plop those roundies.

00:06:25.527 --> 00:06:29.823
All right, step aside.
Time to let my bad boys loose.

00:06:30.949 --> 00:06:34.328
I am Brrr,
devourer of fish and honey!

00:06:39.082 --> 00:06:40.626
I'm coming, darling!

00:06:41.376 --> 00:06:43.920
I shouldn't,
but who's counting?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.007
Help! Fish police!

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.884
Two salmon for dinner?

00:06:49.217 --> 00:06:52.596
What? It's spawning season!
It's a bear holiday!

00:06:52.679 --> 00:06:55.766
That is what you said
when you found those Boy Scouts!

00:06:56.016 --> 00:06:59.061
Next you'll be telling me
I can't crap in the woods!

00:06:59.144 --> 00:07:00.270
That's it!

00:07:00.354 --> 00:07:03.190
We're hibernating
in separate caves this winter!

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.784
My love!

00:07:13.867 --> 00:07:15.744
You made it!

00:07:16.036 --> 00:07:20.082
You overcame salmon instinct
and left your home stream for me!

00:07:21.792 --> 00:07:23.794
So are you gonna
fertilize my eggs now?

00:07:23.877 --> 00:07:26.046
Already taken care of.

00:07:27.255 --> 00:07:30.467
Well, we swam away
and then we came back.

00:07:30.884 --> 00:07:32.844
It's been
an interesting life.

00:07:32.928 --> 00:07:37.808
And the best part is,
it had a happy ending.

00:07:39.393 --> 00:07:43.522
And so the endless
circle of life comes to an end,

00:07:43.605 --> 00:07:45.148
meaningless and grim.

00:07:45.732 --> 00:07:48.235
Why did they live,
and why did they die?

00:07:49.486 --> 00:07:50.570
No reason.

00:07:55.242 --> 00:07:57.661
The isolated
Galapagos Islands.

00:07:57.744 --> 00:08:00.747
A veritable pageant
of evolutionary science.

00:08:00.956 --> 00:08:04.293
Home to dozens of species
found nowhere else,

00:08:04.376 --> 00:08:07.462
such as Darwin's finches
and the marine iguana.

00:08:07.546 --> 00:08:09.464
Also the blue-footed booby!

00:08:09.548 --> 00:08:13.051
That's fairly interesting!
Note the blue coloration of the...

00:08:13.635 --> 00:08:16.054
Of all the creatures
in the Galapagos,

00:08:16.138 --> 00:08:20.309
none is rarer or more tragic
than the Pinta Island tortoise.

00:08:21.018 --> 00:08:24.146
Only a single living specimen
is known to exist,

00:08:24.605 --> 00:08:26.064
Lonesome Hubert.

00:08:26.148 --> 00:08:30.152
Sad news, everyone.
I'm lonesome.

00:08:30.611 --> 00:08:33.405
Hey, would it cheer you up if we gave you
a symbiotic parasite cleaning?

00:08:33.488 --> 00:08:34.865
Would it? Would it?
Would it?

00:08:34.948 --> 00:08:37.909
Fine, knock yourself out.

00:08:38.368 --> 00:08:42.122
The Galapagos finches
eat parasites off the tortoise's skin,

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:44.750
a mutually
beneficial arrangement.

00:08:44.833 --> 00:08:46.251
Except for the parasite!

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.879
How's that, Hubert?
Feeling better?

00:08:49.129 --> 00:08:53.800
A good beaking usually cheers me right
up, but today it's no use.

00:08:54.051 --> 00:08:56.386
My species is as
good as extinct.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:00.140
I haven't seen
a female of my kind in over 100 years!

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.143
There's got to be a lady tortoise
out there for you, Hubert.

00:09:03.226 --> 00:09:04.603
What about her?

00:09:04.978 --> 00:09:09.149
Hey, good lookin',
I've got a lichen that needs a lickin'.

00:09:09.232 --> 00:09:12.861
Are you crazy?
She's a slightly different subspecies!

00:09:13.028 --> 00:09:16.031
See how her shell
flares imperceptibly at the neck?

00:09:16.406 --> 00:09:18.992
Talk about
a cloaca shrinker.

00:09:19.242 --> 00:09:21.036
Well, haven't you
ever met a girl tortoise

00:09:21.119 --> 00:09:24.331
who had that whole
"same subspecies" thing going on?

00:09:24.414 --> 00:09:28.794
Oh my, yes. When I was
a young tortoise of 50,

00:09:28.877 --> 00:09:31.046
I met a hot young
piece of shell

00:09:31.129 --> 00:09:34.383
by a Palo Santo tree on
the far side of the island.

00:09:34.549 --> 00:09:37.594
Let's go look for her!
C'mon, c'mon, c'mon!

00:09:37.678 --> 00:09:41.974
I've always wondered
if she's still there, waiting for me.

00:09:42.057 --> 00:09:44.393
But the trip is far too long.

00:09:44.518 --> 00:09:46.103
It's only 100 feet!

00:09:46.186 --> 00:09:50.649
At my age, it might as well be 200
feet. I'd never make it!

00:09:50.816 --> 00:09:53.568
- Come on, you can make it!
- You can do it!

00:09:54.069 --> 00:09:56.822
Well, let me think it over.

00:09:57.489 --> 00:10:00.367
Let's go already!

00:10:22.556 --> 00:10:23.682
Watch out!

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:28.353
What brings yous to
this part of the isles?

00:10:28.437 --> 00:10:29.896
He's gonna eat us!

00:10:30.147 --> 00:10:31.565
Don't be such a finch.

00:10:31.648 --> 00:10:35.110
We Galapagos tortoises
have no natural predators.

00:10:35.527 --> 00:10:37.279
That's so fascinating!

00:10:54.046 --> 00:10:57.674
I never thought I'd live
to see this tree again.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.177
Thank you for
staying with me, Fry.

00:11:00.469 --> 00:11:03.221
I'm not Fry.
I'm his great-great-grandson, Fry.

00:11:03.513 --> 00:11:05.515
- You are?
- My beak is different, see?

00:11:05.599 --> 00:11:08.352
It evolved a slightly bigger hook
over the generations

00:11:08.435 --> 00:11:10.729
to help me eat the cactus
on this part of the island.

00:11:10.812 --> 00:11:11.939
Watch!

00:11:12.022 --> 00:11:14.107
I'm stuck!

00:11:14.274 --> 00:11:15.317
Oops.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.235
So where's your
lady tortoise, Hubert?

00:11:17.319 --> 00:11:18.946
Lady what?

00:11:19.029 --> 00:11:21.031
Wait, there she is!

00:11:21.114 --> 00:11:23.867
After all these years,
I've found her!

00:11:25.452 --> 00:11:29.373
Oh, my darling!
You haven't aged a day!

00:11:29.915 --> 00:11:31.041
Should we say something?

00:11:31.124 --> 00:11:33.043
Nah. Let him have his fun.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:37.214
All right.
Let's just do what comes naturally.

00:11:37.297 --> 00:11:41.051
I'll get things started
with a little neck extension...

00:11:41.301 --> 00:11:43.261
Then a couple
of these...

00:11:44.763 --> 00:11:46.807
And here we go!

00:11:47.975 --> 00:11:50.852
What the tropical
hell are you doing?

00:11:51.228 --> 00:11:52.771
What?

00:11:52.854 --> 00:11:57.693
I've been saving myself for 100 years,
and this is how you repay me?

00:11:57.776 --> 00:12:00.320
Who is that
hard-shelled skank? I'll kill her!

00:12:00.779 --> 00:12:01.947
Wait, I can explain...

00:12:02.072 --> 00:12:03.240
Shut up!

00:12:03.323 --> 00:12:07.286
I'm going to crack that hussy
open like a slutty Brazil nut!

00:12:14.751 --> 00:12:18.755
This volcanic archipelago
isn't big enough for the both of us.

00:12:23.385 --> 00:12:25.345
Yeah, you'd better topple.

00:12:25.429 --> 00:12:28.724
You always were
a hot-blooded Latina.

00:12:29.057 --> 00:12:32.436
Like all reptiles,
the Galapagos tortoise is cold-blooded.

00:12:32.811 --> 00:12:36.064
Okay, neck, tap, tap,

00:12:36.398 --> 00:12:40.902
climb, climb,
and we're back in business.

00:12:41.737 --> 00:12:44.823
Should we be watching this?
It seems kind of personal.

00:12:44.906 --> 00:12:47.659
That's not an issue for us.
We're wildlife.

00:12:50.787 --> 00:12:53.415
What about the moaning?
Is it okay to listen?

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.751
Sure, but act like
it's no big deal.

00:12:55.876 --> 00:12:58.086
Just pretend
you're eating seeds.

00:13:01.548 --> 00:13:04.468
Is it weird if I talk about
his crazy turtle penis?

00:13:04.843 --> 00:13:05.886
No.

00:13:12.726 --> 00:13:14.853
Well, okay then.

00:13:14.978 --> 00:13:16.855
Yes, it's been lovely.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.482
Hang on a second.

00:13:22.611 --> 00:13:27.282
The Galapagos tortoise lays
a clutch of between six and 15 eggs.

00:13:27.491 --> 00:13:30.452
What do you want?
I'm 150 years old.

00:13:34.831 --> 00:13:36.458
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait!

00:13:36.667 --> 00:13:38.335
Aren't you going
to watch over your young?

00:13:38.627 --> 00:13:41.046
Tortoises don't do that, do we?

00:13:41.129 --> 00:13:42.923
I sure as hell don't.

00:13:43.548 --> 00:13:47.469
Anyway, I've done my part.
The species is saved!

00:13:50.806 --> 00:13:55.143
And so, the survival of
the Pinta Island tortoise is assured.

00:14:10.158 --> 00:14:11.243
Mama!

00:14:13.912 --> 00:14:18.333
And so, the extinction
of the Pinta Island tortoise is assured.

00:14:18.667 --> 00:14:22.671
Two hundred million years
of evolution, snuffed out.

00:14:23.005 --> 00:14:27.342
For, in the end, nature is horrific,
and teaches us nothing.

00:14:27.801 --> 00:14:31.722
Coming up next,
the hilarious antics of the elephant seal,

00:14:31.847 --> 00:14:33.974
the clown of the sea.

00:14:43.358 --> 00:14:45.527
Of all
the spectacles in nature,

00:14:45.819 --> 00:14:48.864
few can match
the mating ritual of the elephant seal.

00:14:48.947 --> 00:14:53.201
Certainly not the salmon.
And the tortoise? Yeah, right.

00:14:53.577 --> 00:14:56.997
The huge, lumbering males
defend patches of beach

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:00.250
to deny their rivals access
to the breeding grounds.

00:15:00.751 --> 00:15:02.586
Just as in human society,

00:15:02.669 --> 00:15:06.965
only the biggest, most obnoxious
males have any chance of mating.

00:15:07.424 --> 00:15:09.801
Aw, yeah!
Survival of the fattest!

00:15:09.885 --> 00:15:12.638
The dominant male,
or "beachmaster,"

00:15:12.804 --> 00:15:15.599
maintains a harem
of up to 50 females.

00:15:15.849 --> 00:15:20.062
Okay, harem, let's get to it.
Form an orderly heap on top of me.

00:15:21.188 --> 00:15:24.316
I like mating with
Beachmaster 'cause he's the largest.

00:15:24.691 --> 00:15:27.694
While the Beachmaster enjoys
the spoils of victory...

00:15:27.819 --> 00:15:30.113
Whoo! I'm doin' it
in my sleep!

00:15:30.197 --> 00:15:33.617
The lesser males languish
at the edge of the colony,

00:15:33.825 --> 00:15:36.703
unable to attract their own
harem due to age...

00:15:36.787 --> 00:15:38.705
Harem?
I can barely see 'em!

00:15:39.039 --> 00:15:40.540
Immaturity...

00:15:40.624 --> 00:15:42.292
I'm scared.

00:15:42.376 --> 00:15:44.044
Or other reasons.

00:15:44.461 --> 00:15:48.882
Hmm. I don't know, does this kelp
scarf make me look fat enough?

00:15:50.759 --> 00:15:54.972
It's so unfair.
That bloated Casanova gets all the ladies!

00:15:55.055 --> 00:15:58.225
Even that one with
the exquisite fat rolls.

00:16:05.732 --> 00:16:08.819
Back off, losers!
Stay away from my beaches!

00:16:08.902 --> 00:16:10.487
You big bully!

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.907
Bite my freshly molted,
blubber-filled ass.

00:16:14.157 --> 00:16:15.826
You're just
a giant lump of fat!

00:16:15.993 --> 00:16:17.703
Do you even have
an ass under there?

00:16:17.786 --> 00:16:20.414
I'm 40% ass!
Arf, arf!

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:21.748
Now beat it!

00:16:21.832 --> 00:16:23.166
Boo!

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.713
With no hope
of defeating the Beachmaster,

00:16:27.796 --> 00:16:31.508
some so-called "sneaky" males
adopt a risky strategy,

00:16:31.591 --> 00:16:33.593
attempting to mate
with one of his harem

00:16:33.719 --> 00:16:35.679
while he is
asleep or distracted.

00:16:36.138 --> 00:16:39.433
So, any of you guys thinking of
being a sneaky male this season?

00:16:41.226 --> 00:16:42.436
This season?

00:16:42.519 --> 00:16:44.563
Walrus don't
need no chicanery.

00:16:44.646 --> 00:16:48.650
Once a lady goes walrus,
she never... She...

00:16:49.109 --> 00:16:51.111
No one ever goes walrus.

00:16:51.403 --> 00:16:56.074
I'm a little old for it now,
but in my prime, I was quite the sneaker.

00:16:56.158 --> 00:16:57.284
How did you do it?

00:16:57.367 --> 00:17:01.204
Well, while the Beachmaster
was off behind a whale carcass,

00:17:01.288 --> 00:17:03.915
loudly fornicating
with my beloved mother,

00:17:04.166 --> 00:17:09.171
I snuck past and surprised my
sweetie with a romantic meal.

00:17:09.421 --> 00:17:11.048
A romantic meal?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.802
The search for food
takes the elephant seal

00:17:15.886 --> 00:17:18.472
to depths few other
mammals can reach.

00:17:22.517 --> 00:17:27.940
In this pitch-black abyss,
life takes on bizarre and horrific forms.

00:17:28.357 --> 00:17:30.359
So, welcome to the abyss.

00:17:31.818 --> 00:17:33.153
Road trip!

00:17:34.988 --> 00:17:36.782
Kill all penguins...

00:17:38.283 --> 00:17:39.868
Kill all penguins.

00:17:41.703 --> 00:17:45.540
What's the matter with you?
You just crushed seven of our babies!

00:17:45.749 --> 00:17:47.709
Yeah, we can
always make more.

00:17:47.793 --> 00:17:50.128
Come on, floozies,
let's repopulate!

00:17:50.629 --> 00:17:55.133
With the Beachmaster occupied,
the sneaky male makes his move.

00:17:57.427 --> 00:17:59.888
I can't believe you came!

00:18:00.222 --> 00:18:02.474
The Beachmaster'll kill you
if he finds out!

00:18:02.724 --> 00:18:04.226
Also, who are you?

00:18:05.269 --> 00:18:08.272
I'm in love with you!
And I don't care what he thinks.

00:18:08.355 --> 00:18:10.232
Here, I brought you
something.

00:18:11.358 --> 00:18:13.944
Hurray! We're three friends at the beach!

00:18:15.904 --> 00:18:18.198
Wait, what's happening, friend?

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:22.577
The female conveys her
receptivity through subtle vocalizations.

00:18:22.661 --> 00:18:23.704
Wanna do it?

00:18:23.912 --> 00:18:25.831
So soon? Oh, well...

00:18:29.668 --> 00:18:33.463
- Sneaky male, eh?
- I thought I told you...

00:18:33.547 --> 00:18:34.881
Oh, my!

00:18:36.508 --> 00:18:37.676
- Well, nice try.
- Better luck next season.

00:18:37.759 --> 00:18:39.344
- You gave it a shot!
- Pathetic.

00:18:48.478 --> 00:18:50.105
Sorry you didn't
get to mate.

00:18:50.188 --> 00:18:52.441
But, hey, we can still
play some beach games.

00:18:52.524 --> 00:18:54.526
Who's up for some Twister?

00:18:54.818 --> 00:18:57.571
No! We beta males
deserve better.

00:18:57.654 --> 00:19:00.699
When we're in charge,
we'll treat females with respect,

00:19:00.782 --> 00:19:03.785
keeping sensible harems
of no more than five.

00:19:03.869 --> 00:19:06.163
And it begins with me.

00:19:07.247 --> 00:19:10.917
Sir, I challenge you
to a duel for control of the beach!

00:19:12.794 --> 00:19:13.962
Aw...

00:19:21.011 --> 00:19:22.971
Hang on...

00:19:29.227 --> 00:19:30.520
Okay, let's fight.

00:19:33.523 --> 00:19:36.443
That's it.
No more Mr. Nice-Jerk.

00:19:44.534 --> 00:19:46.453
The battle
will rage for hours,

00:19:46.536 --> 00:19:49.915
until both males
are exhausted or dead.

00:20:02.844 --> 00:20:04.763
Beachmaster, stop fighting!

00:20:04.846 --> 00:20:06.807
He's been dead since yesterday!

00:20:07.474 --> 00:20:08.934
What? He's dead?

00:20:09.893 --> 00:20:13.981
Whoo! I'm killin' dudes
in my sleep! Yo! Clean up!

00:20:20.529 --> 00:20:24.700
And so, with the threat to the
Beachmaster's supremacy eliminated,

00:20:24.783 --> 00:20:27.244
order is restored
for another year.

00:20:27.536 --> 00:20:32.874
Another year, another generation of
pups fathered by me, Beachmaster.

00:20:36.253 --> 00:20:37.754
I'm the greatest, baby!

00:20:37.838 --> 00:20:39.881
You go, Beachmaster!

00:20:40.674 --> 00:20:44.428
And so concludes
our exploration of planet Earth.

00:20:44.511 --> 00:20:47.431
For a holographic
brain injection of tonight's program,

00:20:47.514 --> 00:20:51.560
send $5 to this station,
care of me, the narrator.

00:20:51.893 --> 00:20:52.936
Good night.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:57.149
Mutual of Omicron.
Have you insured your planet?